      ":question/problem": "Suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=⟨{t}^{4}-6{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le 4.$\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-4$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=16,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨256{u}^{4}-96{u}^{2},\\,4u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
