  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186162083,
      "id": "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65",
      "title": "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a6464870-75eb-51df-ac18-31b98b4d1e77",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=9$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(u)=⟨8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{u}{4}),\\,8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{u}{4})⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 4\\pi .$ \n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=108,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(t)=⟨8\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,8\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi}{3} .$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-9$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=9$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=9.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we note that both parameterizations traverse a half-circle of radius $8$ centered at $O$ between $0$ and $\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "25b35edb-aac4-55f0-80ab-4b95c79a84ad",
